### Write-only token

Use `token_wo` to supply an authentication token without storing it in plan or
state files. It accepts ephemeral values, including values fetched from a
secret manager's ephemeral resource. This requires Terraform 1.11+ or OpenTofu
1.11+.

{{ tffile (printf "examples/resources/%s/write_only.tf" .Name)}}

Set `token_wo_version` alongside `token_wo` and increment it when rotating the
token. Changing only `token_wo` does not trigger an update because its previous
value is not retained. The provider sends the current token on creation and
every configuration update, including updates to other arguments.

To migrate an existing resource, replace `token` with `token_wo` and set
`token_wo_version`. Applying removes the old `token` value from the current
resource state without replacing the logstream configuration. Previous state
snapshots and saved plans still contain any tokens they previously recorded.
The secret's source must also avoid persisting its value; a regular secret
data source still stores its results in state.

After importing a resource, configure `token_wo` and `token_wo_version` to manage
its token. The API does not return the token or its version.

